======================================================================
GRAND SYNTHESIS
======================================================================

The most promising reframes for new proof routes:

1. TOPOLOGICAL (odd/even parity complementarity):
   Every odd-speed runner is safe at t or at t+1/2.
   This gives a FREE lower bound on the all-safe measure.
   For small n with many odd speeds, this may already prove LRC!

2. SPECTRAL (Fourier):
   If the DC component exceeds the sum of AC components,
   L(t) > 0 for some t.  Computable and tight for small n.

3. LOVÁSZ LOCAL LEMMA:
   The dependency structure of runner-close events is sparse
   for coprime speed sets.  May prove LRC for large max_speed/n.

4. RELATIVISTIC:
   Rapidity threshold = 0.5*ln(n-1) gives a natural scale.
   The formal group F(x,y)=(x+y)/(1+xy) is additive in rapidity.
   This connects to the project's central object.

